1908–09 was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 21st season of football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1900/celtic1909.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1908-09|website=Londonhearts.com|access-date=1 August 2018}}</ref> They won the league for the fifth time in a row, which was a record at the time.

Celtic also reached [[1909 Scottish Cup final|the final of the Scottish Cup]] against fellow Glasgow team [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]]. After a 2–2 draw on 10 April, a replay on 17 April also ended in a draw, 1-1. Crowd disorder after it was announced that extra time was only provided in the event of a second replay caused serious damage at [[Hampden Park]], as well as over 100 injured. Both clubs requested the SFA not schedule a second replay and subsequently, the trophy and medals were withheld, with no winner ever declared.

Celtic also reached the finals of both the [[Glasgow Cup]] and the [[Glasgow Merchants Charity Cup|Glasgow Merchants' Charity Cup]], but lost both: the Glasgow Cup to [[Third Lanark A.C.|Third Lanark]] 4–0 after two replays; and the Charity Cup to Rangers, 4–2.

